# System Hardware & Components Specification

## 1. Electrochemical Core (VRFB Stack)
* **Vanadium Electrolyte:** Aqueous $V^{2+}/V^{3+}$ and $V^{4+}/V^{5+}$ solutions.
* **Proton Exchange Membrane (PEM):** (e.g., Nafion or custom ion-exchange membrane).
* **Graphite Felt Electrodes & Bipolar Plates:** Conductive current collection with chemical resistance.

## 2. Thermal & Hydraulic Loop (The "Blood Circulatory" System)
* **Electrolyte Storage Tanks:** Chemically inert (HDPE/PVDF) storage vessels.
* **Variable-Speed Chemical Pumps:** Magnetic-drive pumps resistant to acidic solutions.
* **Heat Exchangers / Cold Plates:** Direct-to-chip microchannel cooling blocks attached to server heat loads.
* **Sensors & Telemetry:** Flow meters, pH sensors, thermocouples, and pressure transducers.

## 3. Power Electronics & Control
* **Bidirectional DC-DC Converters:** Manages charge/discharge voltage to server bus bars.
* **BMS / Microcontroller:** (e.g., ESP32, Raspberry Pi, or PLC) reading telemetry and controlling pump speeds via scripts in `/scripts`.
